# 3. USER ROLES AND PERMISSIONS

The application must support exactly two roles initially.

## 3.1 ADMIN

Admin has complete administrative access.

Admin permissions:

- View team-wide work entries.
- View individual member work history.
- View daily submission status.
- Create and manage team members.
- Activate and deactivate member accounts.
- Assign Admin or Member roles.
- Configure dynamic work logging fields.
- Configure field types and validation rules.
- Configure work categories and statuses.
- Manage sprint information.
- Associate and review sprint-related work.
- View daily, weekly and monthly reports.
- Generate and copy weekly team summaries.
- Reopen submitted daily reports when necessary.
- Configure company timezone and working days.
- View audit logs.
- Access system settings.
- Preview the Member experience.

Admin does not need to approve daily submissions.

## 3.2 MEMBER

Member permissions:

- Sign in using an approved company Google account.
- View their daily work.
- Add multiple work entries.
- Edit their own entries before daily submission.
- View their own work history.
- View team-wide work summaries.
- Associate work with an available sprint.
- Add optional Azure DevOps ticket references.
- Complete their daily submission.
- View their profile.

Members cannot:

- Configure application fields.
- Modify system settings.
- Change roles.
- Access Admin-only operations.
- Modify another member's work entries.
- Reopen submitted reports.

## 3.3 Permission Enforcement

IMPORTANT:

Permissions must be enforced on the backend for every protected API.

Hiding buttons or navigation items in React is not sufficient.

Changing a role value in the browser must never grant additional permissions.

