# 6. DYNAMIC WORK LOGGING CONFIGURATION

## 6.1 Objective

Admin must be able to configure the work logging form without requiring any source-code changes or application redeployment.

The Member's Add Work form must be generated dynamically using the latest active Admin configuration.

## 6.2 Configurable Field Properties

Every field must support:

| Property | Description |
|---|---|
| Field name | Display label |
| Field type | Input type |
| Required | Mandatory or optional |
| Placeholder | Input guidance |
| Help text | Additional instructions |
| Options | Dropdown or selection values |
| Validation | Length, format or value rules |
| Display order | Position in the form |
| Active status | Enabled or disabled |
| Default value | Optional initial value |

## 6.3 Supported Field Types

The initial release must support:

1. Short Text
2. Long Text
3. Dropdown
4. Multi-select
5. Radio Button
6. Checkbox
7. Date
8. URL
9. Number

## 6.4 Recommended Initial Fields

These are initial defaults that Admin can modify.

| Field | Type | Required |
|---|---|---|
| Work Summary | Long Text | Yes |
| Work Category | Dropdown | Yes |
| Description / Details | Long Text | Configurable |
| Work Status | Dropdown | Yes |
| Sprint | Dropdown | Optional |
| ADO Ticket Reference | URL or Short Text | Optional |
| Blocker / Dependency | Long Text | Optional |
| Additional Notes | Long Text | Optional |

## 6.5 Default Work Categories

- Development
- Bug Fix
- Code Review
- Testing
- Research
- Meeting
- Deployment
- Support
- Documentation
- Other

Admin must be able to add, rename, reorder, disable and modify these options.

## 6.6 Default Work Statuses

- Completed
- In Progress
- Blocked

Admin can configure the available statuses.

IMPORTANT:

The weekly summary generator must use the configured status values and their defined meanings. It must not guess whether work is completed based on the description.

## 6.7 Dynamic Configuration Rules

- Every field must have a stable unique ID.
- Existing work entries must retain their original values.
- Changing a field label must not destroy historical data.
- Field types must not be changed incompatibly without a migration or compatibility rule.
- Disabled fields must remain available for historical display.
- Deleted fields should be archived instead of permanently removed.
- Mandatory fields must be validated on the frontend and backend.
- Invalid values must be rejected by the backend.
- Configuration changes must be audited.
- Members must not be able to modify field definitions.

IMPORTANT:

Implement configuration versioning.

Every work entry should retain the configuration version used when it was created. Historical records must remain readable even after Admin changes the form.

# 7. DAILY WORK LOGGING

## 7.1 Work Entry Workflow

1. Member signs in.
2. Member opens My Work.
3. Application displays the current work date.
4. Member clicks Add Work.
5. Application loads the active dynamic form configuration.
6. Member enters the required details.
7. Member optionally adds an ADO reference.
8. Member saves the entry.
9. Saved work appears immediately in My Work.
10. Member can add more work entries.
11. Member completes the daily submission.

## 7.2 Work Entry Rules

IMPORTANT:

- Multiple entries per day must be supported.
- No start time field.
- No end time field.
- No duration field.
- No time-spent field.
- No working-hour calculations.
- No expected daily hours.
- Backend generates timestamps.
- Backend determines authenticated member ownership.
- Work date must be validated using the configured timezone.
- Members cannot assign entries to another user.
- Every create, edit and correction must be auditable.
- Save operations must not silently fail.

## 7.3 Editing Rules

Before daily submission:

- Members can edit their own work entries.
- Members can correct descriptions and configured field values.
- Members can delete their own entries if deletion is permitted by system policy.
- Changes must be recorded in the audit log.

After daily submission:

- Member editing is locked.
- Admin can reopen the report.
- Any correction must be traceable.
- Original and updated values should be retained where appropriate.

# 8. DAILY SUBMISSION

Daily submission must be strict.

The Member must complete their daily report.

## 8.1 Complete Day Workflow

Provide one clear action:

**Complete Day**

Before submission, the backend must validate:

- At least one valid work entry exists, unless a no-work reason is supplied.
- All mandatory fields are completed.
- All field values match their configured types.
- Work entries belong to the authenticated member.
- The work date is valid.
- The report has not already been submitted.

If validation fails, show clear errors.

## 8.2 After Submission

- Mark the daily report as Submitted.
- Lock normal Member editing.
- Show a clear submission confirmation.
- Preserve all submitted entries.
- Allow Admin to reopen when necessary.
- Record the submitter and timestamp.

IMPORTANT:

Daily submission completion is different from completing every work item.

A Member may submit a daily report containing both Completed and In Progress work.

No Admin approval is required.

## 8.3 No-Work Days

Allow a Member to submit a no-work reason when no work entries exist.

The reason must be validated according to the configured minimum requirements.

Do not generate fabricated work entries.

