# 21. MANDATORY ACCEPTANCE AND TESTING CRITERIA

The application must not be considered complete just because all screens are available.

Every requirement must be functionally tested.

## 21.1 Authentication and Security

- Approved Workspace accounts can sign in.
- Unapproved accounts cannot sign in.
- Personal accounts cannot bypass domain restrictions.
- Members cannot access Admin APIs.
- Members cannot edit another member's entries.
- Deactivated users cannot access the system.
- Frontend manipulation cannot bypass backend permissions.
- Sessions expire securely.

## 21.2 Dynamic Work Configuration

- Admin can create every supported field type.
- Required fields are enforced.
- Dropdown and multi-select options work.
- Field ordering is respected.
- Disabled fields are handled correctly.
- Configuration changes do not destroy old records.
- Historical records display their original values.
- Invalid API payloads are rejected.

## 21.3 Work Logging

- Multiple entries can be added on one day.
- Work entries persist after refresh and re-login.
- ADO references work correctly.
- Editing updates the correct entry.
- Ownership cannot be manipulated.
- Work dates remain accurate across timezone boundaries.
- No time or duration fields are introduced.

## 21.4 Daily Submission

- Valid reports can be submitted.
- Invalid reports are rejected.
- Empty reports require a valid no-work reason.
- Duplicate submissions are prevented.
- Submitted reports are locked.
- Admin can reopen a report.
- Reopening and corrections are audited.
- Work entries are not lost during submission.

## 21.5 Sprint Management

- Admin can create and edit sprints.
- Members can associate work with the correct sprint.
- Sprint summaries use actual saved entries.
- Archived sprints remain visible in historical records.
- No ticket-management functionality is introduced.

## 21.6 Weekly Summary

- Admin can select the correct reporting week.
- Only eligible work entries are included.
- Completed work appears under Work Completed.
- Ongoing work appears under Work In Progress.
- Employee names are excluded.
- Work dates and weekly date ranges are excluded.
- No third category is generated.
- Duplicate descriptions are handled.
- Technical terminology is preserved.
- No invented achievements appear.
- The generated output matches actual work logs.
- Copy action works correctly.
- Empty and error states are handled.

## 21.7 Reporting Accuracy

- Member totals match the underlying records.
- Team totals match the sum of eligible member records.
- Daily reports use the correct timezone.
- Weekly and monthly filters are accurate.
- Sprint summaries match associated work entries.
- Dashboard and report calculations agree.
- No stale or hardcoded values are displayed.

## 21.8 Reliability

- Simultaneous requests do not overwrite data.
- Retried requests do not create duplicates.
- Failed saves are clearly reported.
- Partial failures are handled safely.
- Backup and recovery procedures work.
- Audit records are preserved.
- Historical data remains available.

